Configs:  swi_f.cfg, stk_a.cfg (running-config after setup; saved to startup: no)

VERDICT: PASS -- an 802.1Q trunk built as a static aggregator carries line-rate traffic from many source MACs with no 4-byte deficit
      static aggregator sa2, 2 links ...... up  (x230 sa2 = port1.0.2 + port1.0.3, trunk, VLAN 106 tagged)
      1518-byte frames eth3 -> eth1 ....... PASS  (813001 / 813001 at exact length, 999.8 Mbps on the wire)
      1518-byte frames eth1 -> eth3 ....... PASS  (812501 / 812501 at exact length, 999.6 Mbps on the wire)
      1500-byte frames eth3 -> eth1 ....... PASS  (822501 / 822501 at exact length, 999.7 Mbps on the wire)
      64 source MACs over both links ...... 50/50  (x230 per-member counters, each direction)
      drops on any x230 port .............. 0
CAVEAT:  No Ixia on tb470: tools/linerate.py (tcpreplay) on tb470's 1G NICs stands in, with 64
         rotating source MACs per sender. "No 4 byte deficit" is proven end to end: every frame
         left the far access port at exactly the length sent after crossing the tagged trunk; the
         tagged frames on the trunk links themselves were not captured. Small frames and VLANs
         other than 106 were not sent.

