STEP 1 -- "The 802.1Q trunked port should work equally as well being a static
           Aggregator. Multiple source mac addresses should be sent from the
           Ixia"                                                            PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Expected: "There should be no 4 byte deficit per frame in traffic flow"
  Method: maximum standard untagged frames (1518 bytes on the wire) cross the tagged trunk and
  must arrive at the far access port at exactly the length sent; every receive count uses
  --rx-len. Top rate, 10 s, 64 source MACs per sender, both directions, then 1500-byte frames.
  The x230's per-member counters, read between the runs, show how the aggregator spreads the
  source MACs over its two links.
